== Canon is not erasure ==

A canonical V2 page is a current orientation point. It does not make earlier formulations worthless or retroactively identical.

For foundational writing, preserve:
* distinctive language that carries meaning;
* changes in philosophical position;
* changes in governance assumptions;
* abandoned or superseded implementation claims;
* metaphors and conceptual models when they materially shaped the system;
* reasons for revision where recoverable.

The exact current public V1 bodies and complete public revision histories are preserved under <code>archive-v1/</code>. Historical material can therefore be quoted, compared, or restored without relying on memory.

== Charter lineage ==

The V1 corpus contains three materially different Charter traditions:

=== Epistemic / field Charter ===
[[BITwiki Charter]] developed the language of radical epistemic humility, confidence trails, radical skepticism, hyper-realism, nullification of non-signals, purposeful recursion, field coherence, machine readability, human legibility, interoperability, and long-term preservation.

=== Research-space Charter ===
[[BITwiki Charter Revised]] framed BITwiki as a professional research space rather than an authoritative source. It emphasized radical realism, direct assessment over pedigree, context-dependent evidence, multiple methods of inquiry, explicit BITCORE curation, and the historical BITHUB→agent→BITwiki authorship model.

=== Performative / holographic Charter ===
The separate V1 [[Charter]] explored BITwiki as a "holographic projection of symbiotic knowledge": observer-participation, H=1 human–AI symbiosis, fractal self-similarity, provisionality markers, falsification/death conditions, knowledge flow, and resistance to rigidification.

V2 preserves this as a distinct philosophical branch. It is not silently converted into literal scientific fact, and it is not discarded merely because its language is unusual.

== Constitutional relationship ==

The Charter states how BITwiki intends to conduct knowledge work. The Constitution states the constraints that should remain true even as specific workflows, schemas, models, extensions, and interfaces change.

The Manifestos establish direction. The Charter establishes commitments. The Constitution establishes invariants. The Foundational Triad supplies a recurring analytical frame.

== Editorial rule ==

<pre>
recover exact source
→ compare revisions and parallel formulations
→ identify durable meaning, historical context, and implementation assumptions
→ preserve strong authored language
→ separate current canon from historical branch
→ make new connective prose explicit and minimal
</pre>

See [[BITwiki:Source lineage]], [[BITwiki:Editorial protocol]], and [[BITwiki:V1 public corpus inventory]].

